<title>BRAZIL: Petrobras plans to launch Level One ADRs.</title>
<headline>Petrobras plans to launch Level One ADRs.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's state oil company Petrobras said it plans to launch Level One American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) by year's end.  </p>
<p>A Petrobras spokeswoman said Citibank will be the depositary of Petrobras shares in the U.S.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman also said the company was authorized to issue $250 million in three-year Eurobonds this year.</p>
<p>Petrobras' last Eurobond issue was in October 1995, when the firm launched $150 million in bonds in the Japanese market, she added.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
